--   The packed row addition is the selected-bit address map of rowAddr
-- statement:
--   **The packed row addition is the selected-bit address map of `rowAddr`.**
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.KFRAddr`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem NLogN.KFR.encode_rowAddAddr (hK : 1 ≤ K) {q : ℕ} (hq : q < B * 2 ^ t * S0) {px py : Fin 3}
--       {i j : Fin m} (hi : σ px = i) (hj : σ py = j) (hij : i ≠ j) :
--       ((encode (NLogN.KFR.shR K (m ^ k) e t S0 B σ)
--           (rowAddAddr K (e % K) (m ^ k) px py (decode (NLogN.KFR.shR K (m ^ k) e t S0 B σ) q)) : ℕ) : ℤ) =
--         fsetZ (fun p => 2 ^ pos p * S0) q (rowAddr i j (fbit (fun p => 2 ^ pos p * S0) q))
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** The lemma belongs to the part *KFR: the packed rectangle of three rows, and the row addition as `rowAddAddr`*: For a stride-`K` family `pos` (`pos (r, c) + K (c + f r) = e`, `f = m^k`) and three rows
--   `σ 0 < σ 1 < σ 2`, `shR` is the rectangle `rect N0 N1 N2 N3 (fK)` whose chunk slot `τ` is the
--   field of row `σ τ` (weight `2^{sR (σ τ)} S₀`).  **`encode_rowAddAddr`**: on this rectangle, the
--   address map `rowAddAddr K (e mod K) f px py` is `fset (rowAddr (σ px) (σ py))`.
